<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Open Science</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To support the evaluation of this paper’s core contributions, we provide the following artifacts:</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Ax1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Source Code:</span> Full implementation of the proposed BI-BAU defense method and evaluation pipeline.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Configuration Files:</span> Model settings, hyperparameters, and experimental setups.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scripts and Documentation:</span> Scripts for running experiments, reproducing results, and accompanying README with usage instructions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Environment:</span> Conda environment file (‘requirements.yml‘) specifying dependencies for replication.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">All artifacts are accessible to the program committee via the anonymous repository: <a href="https://anonymous.4open.science/r/BI-BAU-0634/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://anonymous.4open.science/r/BI-BAU-0634/</a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">All artifacts contain no identifying information to ensure compliance with double-blind review.
No restricted or sensitive data are included. The provided materials allow the program committee to fully reproduce the main experimental results reported in the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Organization of the Appendix</h2>

<div id="Ax2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For clarity and ease of navigation, the Appendix is organized as follows:
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
<ul id="Ax2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Section <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Summary of Symbols ‣ Rethinking Backdoor Adversarial Unlearning through the Lens of Catastrophic Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a></span> provides a summary of the symbols used throughout the paper.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Section <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Theoretical Proof ‣ Rethinking Backdoor Adversarial Unlearning through the Lens of Catastrophic Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a></span> presents the theoretical proofs included in this work.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Section <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Extending BI-BAU to Multi-Modal Contrastive Learning ‣ Rethinking Backdoor Adversarial Unlearning through the Lens of Catastrophic Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a></span> details the implementation of extending BI-BAU to multi-modal
contrastive learning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Section <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Additional Implementation Details ‣ Rethinking Backdoor Adversarial Unlearning through the Lens of Catastrophic Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a></span> describes additional implementation details for the experiments.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Section <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Additional Experiments ‣ Rethinking Backdoor Adversarial Unlearning through the Lens of Catastrophic Forgetting in Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a></span> presents complementary experimental results.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
